      "description": "<p>Latest poll shows 0.3-point gap between left and right blocs, with country’s reputation as global champion of human rights said to be at stake</p><p>Sweden goes to the polls on Sunday in an extremely close election that could see the far right enter government for the first time if the country’s rightwing parties can form a majority.</p><p>Opinion polls show the centre-left opposition alliance ahead, with Magdalena ⁠Andersson of the Social Democrats the favourite to become prime minister again after four years in opposition, but her bloc’s lead has narrowed considerably in the final days of the campaign.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/12/sweden-extremely-close-election-could-see-far-right-enter-government\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
